---
import DocsNav from "../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import {
  evidenceHighlights,
  evidenceRows,
  records,
  sourceUrl,
} from "../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Evidence — OrbitKV"
  description="Recorded correctness, runtime behavior, performance boundaries, and open qualification work for OrbitKV."
  active="Evidence"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence &amp; qualification</p>
    <h1>Progress you can inspect.</h1>
    <p>
      Every result belongs to its source revision, model, hardware, and
      workload. These records show what has been tested and where the next work
      begins.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Evidence" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The latest device qualification</h2>
      <p>
        On 14 September 2026, the H20 qualification exercised the primary
        Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 text checkpoint, FlashInfer and FlashAttention-3
        candidates, strict artifact replay, and HTTP shutdown with active
        requests.
      </p>
      <div class="metric-grid">
        {evidenceHighlights.map((item) => (
          <article>
            <strong>{item.value}</strong>
            <h3>{item.label}</h3>
            <p>{item.detail}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p>
        The recorded decode representative selected FlashInfer tensor-core
        attention; the packed-prefill representative selected FlashAttention-3.
        The 96 full-vocabulary comparisons reached a maximum absolute error of
        0.71875 under the existing 1.0 gate. The HTTP runs matched the
        independent token reference and returned all 64 KV pages and both
        fixed-state pools to free state.
      </p>
      <p>
        Warm full-logit decode measured about 24.1 ms in this diagnostic. This
        run establishes no whole-model speedup against another backend or
        engine. Inspect the{" "}
        <a href={sourceUrl("results/provider-kernels-20260914/README.md")}>
          full report, limits, and source identities
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <h2>Where the implementation stands</h2>
      <div
        class="table-scroll"
        tabindex="0"
        role="region"
        aria-label="Scrollable capability table"
      >
        <table class="data-table evidence-data">
          <caption>Current capability and qualification boundaries</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Surface</th>
              <th scope="col">Status</th>
              <th scope="col">Evidence &amp; scope</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {evidenceRows.map((item) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{item.surface}</td>
                <td>
                  <span class="status-tag">{item.status}</span>
                </td>
                <td>
                  {item.detail}
                  <small>{item.boundary}</small>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2>Selected records</h2>
      <div class="record-list">
        {records.map((record) => (
          <article class="record">
            <div class="record-meta">
              <time datetime={record.date.replaceAll(".", "-")}>
                {record.date}
              </time>
              <span class="status-tag">{record.tag}</span>
            </div>
            <h3>
              <a href={sourceUrl(record.path)}>
                {record.name}
                <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
            </h3>
            <p>{record.detail}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p>
        The <a href={sourceUrl("results/README.md")}>complete evidence index</a>{" "}
        also retains lifecycle, graph residency, compiler attribution, and
        matched serving comparisons. Historical records keep their original
        source and workload scope.
      </p>
      <h2>Performance is still an open question</h2>
      <p>
        Same-executor experiments have demonstrated lower live KV payload and
        improvements from compiler selection. Recorded comparisons against vLLM
        and SGLang still show a serving performance gap. A successful kernel
        test or warm artifact replay does not settle end-to-end throughput.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Attribute execution and search costs on the primary 27B workload.
        </li>
        <li>
          Compare throughput, p95 time to first token, and inter-token latency
          under matched load.
        </li>
        <li>
          Extend batch, context, memory-pressure, and long-running reuse
          coverage.
        </li>
        <li>
          Qualify new state layouts, attention families, and external transports
          independently.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        See the{" "}
        <a href={sourceUrl("docs/benchmarking.md")}>measurement method</a> and{" "}
        <a href={sourceUrl("docs/roadmap.md")}>roadmap</a> for the acceptance
        criteria.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
